my name is Michel de Graaff and I've  been teaching in linguistics at MIT for  the past 21 years already and I'm the  faculty instructor for the course on  clear languages and Caribbean identities  so my research is about trying to  understand how languages evolve over  time and what happens when new languages  are created say for example the  Caribbean in magnitude Haiti where  Haitian Creole emerged in the seventeen  eighteenth century so we try to  understand the patterns of development  of the things that we call Creole  languages and in terms of the structure  but also have an applied side to my work  where I try to understand how best to  use say Haitian Creole and other local  languages in education and how that's  crucial for development of countries  like Haiti
 

